{"id":"mahabharata-2-053","work":"mahabharata","part":2,"partName":"सभापर्व","partNameEn":"Sabha Parva","unit":53,"title":"त्रिपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 53 · The game begins","summary":{"en":"In the gaming hall Shakuni invites Yudhishthira to play. Yudhishthira objects that cheating is sinful, but bound by his vow never to refuse a challenge, he sits down to play Shakuni, who throws for Duryodhana, and Shakuni wins the first stake.","kn":"ಜೂಜಿನ ಸಭೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಶಕುನಿ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನನ್ನು ಆಡಲು ಕರೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಮೋಸ ಪಾಪವೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಆಕ್ಷೇಪಿಸಿದರೂ ಸವಾಲನ್ನು ತಿರಸ್ಕರಿಸದ ವ್ರತಕ್ಕೆ ಬದ್ಧನಾಗಿ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಪರವಾಗಿ ಆಡುವ ಶಕುನಿಯೊಂದಿಗೆ ಕುಳಿತುಕೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಮೊದಲ ಪಣವನ್ನು ಶಕುನಿ ಗೆಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"द्यूत-सभा में शकुनि युधिष्ठिर को खेलने बुलाता है। युधिष्ठिर आपत्ति करते हैं कि छल पाप है, पर चुनौती अस्वीकार न करने के व्रत से बँधे वे दुर्योधन की ओर से पासा फेंकने वाले शकुनि के साथ बैठते हैं, और शकुनि पहला दाँव जीत लेता है।","te":"జూదసభలో శకుని యుధిష్ఠిరుని ఆడడానికి పిలుస్తాడు. మోసం పాపమని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అభ్యంతరపెట్టినా సవాలును తిరస్కరించని వ్రతానికి కట్టుబడి దుర్యోధనుని తరఫున పాచికలు వేసే శకునితో కూర్చుంటాడు; మొదటి పందెం శకుని గెలుస్తాడు.","ta":"சூது மண்டபத்தில் ஶகுனி யுதிஷ்டிரரை ஆட அழைக்கிறான். வஞ்சனை பாவம் என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் மறுத்தாலும், சவாலை மறுக்காத விரதத்துக்குக் கட்டுப்பட்டுத் துரியோதனனுக்காகப் பகடை உருட்டும் ஶகுனியுடன் அமர, முதல் பந்தயத்தை ஶகுனி வெல்கிறான்.","ml":"ചൂതുശാലയിൽ കളിക്കാൻ ശകുനി യുധിഷ്ഠിരനെ ക്ഷണിക്കുന്നു. വഞ്ചന പാപമാണെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ എതിർക്കുന്നു, എങ്കിലും വെല്ലുവിളി ഒരിക്കലും നിരസിക്കില്ലെന്ന പ്രതിജ്ഞയാൽ ബന്ധിതനായി അദ്ദേഹം ശകുനിയോടൊപ്പം കളിക്കാനിരിക്കുന്നു; ദുര്യോധനന് വേണ്ടി എറിയുന്ന ശകുനി ആദ്യ പണയം വിജയിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 2.53; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Apr 19 2006","sections":[{"title":"द्यूतपर्व","titleEn":"Dyuta Parva (The dice game)","verses":[{"text":"शकुनिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"उपस्तीर्णा सभा राजन्रन्तुं चैते कृतक्षणाः ।\nअक्षानुप्त्वा देवनस्य समयोऽस्तु युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"The hall is spread with seats, king, and these men have set aside the time to play. Let the dice be cast and the terms of play be agreed, Yudhishthira."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"निकृतिर्देवनं पापं न क्षात्रोऽत्र पराक्रमः ।\nन च नीतिर्ध्रुवा राजन्किं त्वं द्यूतं प्रशंससि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gambling is cheating and sin; there is no kshatriya valor in it and no firm policy. King, why do you praise dice?"}},{"n":3,"text":"न हि मानं प्रशंसन्ति निकृतौ कितवस्य ह ।\nशकुने मैव नो जैषीरमार्गेण नृशंसवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They do not praise a gambler's pride in his trickery. Shakuni, do not defeat us by a crooked path like a cruel man."}},{"text":"शकुनिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"योऽन्वेति संख्यां निकृतौ विधिज्ञ-\nश्चेष्टास्वखिन्नः कितवोऽक्षजासु ।\nमहामतिर्यश्च जानाति द्यूतं\nस वै सर्वं सहते प्रक्रियासु ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gambler who follows the count in a cheat, knows the method and is not wearied by the efforts of dice, and who is of great intelligence and knows the game, can bear everything in its procedures."}},{"n":5,"text":"अक्षग्लहः सोऽभिभवेत्परं न-\nस्तेनैव कालो भवतीदमात्थ ।\nदीव्यामहे पार्थिव मा विशङ्कां\nकुरुष्व पाणं च चिरं च मा कृथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The stake at dice may overcome the other side, but it is the time that does that to us; so you say. Let us play, king; have no doubt, place the wager, and do not delay."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"एवमाहायमसितो देवलो मुनिसत्तमः ।\nइमानि लोकद्वाराणि यो वै संचरते सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage Asita Devala, best of munis, who always wanders through these gates of the world, spoke thus."}},{"n":7,"text":"इदं वै देवनं पापं मायया कितवैः सह ।\nधर्मेण तु जयो युद्धे तत्परं साधु देवनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This gambling with deceitful gamblers is sinful. But to win in battle by righteous means is the best kind of game."}},{"n":8,"text":"नार्या म्लेच्छन्ति भाषाभिर्मायया न चरन्त्युत ।\nअजिह्ममशठं युद्धमेतत्सत्पुरुषव्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Noble people do not speak foreign tongues to mislead nor act by trickery. A straight, honest fight is the vow of good men."}},{"n":9,"text":"शक्तितो ब्राह्मणान्वन्द्याञ्शिक्षितुं प्रयतामहे ।\nतद्वै वित्तं मातिदेवीर्मा जैषीः शकुने परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We strive as we can to support brahmins who deserve homage. Shakuni, do not win from us that wealth by overplaying."}},{"n":10,"text":"नाहं निकृत्या कामये सुखान्युत धनानि वा ।\nकितवस्याप्यनिकृतेर्वृत्तमेतन्न पूज्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not desire pleasures or wealth got by cheating. Even a gambler's honest conduct is not praised if it is crooked."}},{"text":"शकुनिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"श्रोत्रियोऽश्रोत्रियमुत निकृत्यैव युधिष्ठिर ।\nविद्वानविदुषोऽभ्येति नाहुस्तां निकृतिं जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, a learned man defeats an unlearned one, and a scholar of the Vedas beats a non-scholar, and people do not call that cheating."}},{"n":12,"text":"एवं त्वं मामिहाभ्येत्य निकृतिं यदि मन्यसे ।\nदेवनाद्विनिवर्तस्व यदि ते विद्यते भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you think that this is cheating when you come against me, then withdraw from play, if you are afraid."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"आहूतो न निवर्तेयमिति मे व्रतमाहितम् ।\nविधिश्च बलवान्राजन्दिष्टस्यास्मि वशे स्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have taken the vow not to turn back when called. Destiny is strong, king, and I stand under fate's power."}},{"n":14,"text":"अस्मिन्समागमे केन देवनं मे भविष्यति ।\nप्रतिपाणश्च कोऽन्योऽस्ति ततो द्यूतं प्रवर्तताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this gathering, with whom shall my game be, and who else has a stake to match? Let the play begin."}},{"text":"दुर्योधन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"अहं दातास्मि रत्नानां धनानां च विशां पते ।\nमदर्थे देविता चायं शकुनिर्मातुलो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will provide the jewels and wealth, lord of the people, and my uncle Shakuni will play on my behalf."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"अन्येनान्यस्य विषमं देवनं प्रतिभाति मे ।\nएतद्विद्वन्नुपादत्स्व काममेवं प्रवर्तताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It seems to me an unequal game, one person playing for another. Wise one, understand this, and let it go on as you like."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"उपोह्यमाने द्यूते तु राजानः सर्व एव ते ।\nधृतराष्ट्रं पुरस्कृत्य विविशुस्तां सभां ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the game was being set up, all those kings, with Dhritarashtra before them, entered the hall."}},{"n":18,"text":"भीष्मो द्रोणः कृपश्चैव विदुरश्च महामतिः ।\nनातीवप्रीतमनसस्तेऽन्ववर्तन्त भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, Drona, Kripa and the very wise Vidura followed, Bharata, though their minds were not very pleased."}},{"n":19,"text":"ते द्वंद्वशः पृथक्चैव सिंहग्रीवा महौजसः ।\nसिंहासनानि भूरीणि विचित्राणि च भेजिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those mighty lion-necked men sat in pairs and separately on many fine, varied thrones."}},{"n":20,"text":"शुशुभे सा सभा राजन्राजभिस्तैः समागतैः ।\nदेवैरिव महाभागैः समवेतैस्त्रिविष्टपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That hall shone with the assembled kings, like heaven with the gathered great gods."}},{"n":21,"text":"सर्वे वेदविदः शूराः सर्वे भास्वरमूर्तयः ।\nप्रावर्तत महाराज सुहृद्द्यूतमनन्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All were Veda-knowers and heroes, all of shining form. Then the friendly game of dice began, great king."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"अयं बहुधनो राजन्सागरावर्तसंभवः ।\nमणिर्हारोत्तरः श्रीमान्कनकोत्तमभूषणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, this jewel of great value, born in the ocean's whirl, strung in a necklace and splendid, adorned with the finest gold, is my wealth."}},{"n":23,"text":"एतद्राजन्धनं मह्यं प्रतिपाणस्तु कस्तव ।\nभवत्वेष क्रमस्तात जयाम्येनं दुरोदरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That is my wealth, king; what is your stake against it? Let this be the order of play, and I will win this gambler."}},{"text":"दुर्योधन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":24,"text":"सन्ति मे मणयश्चैव धनानि विविधानि च ।\nमत्सरश्च न मेऽर्थेषु जयाम्येनं दुरोदरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have jewels and many kinds of wealth, and I do not begrudge my riches. I will beat this man at dice."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"ततो जग्राह शकुनिस्तानक्षानक्षतत्त्ववित् ।\nजितमित्येव शकुनिर्युधिष्ठिरमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shakuni, expert in the truth of dice, took up the dice and said to Yudhishthira, I have won."}}]}]}